This crate wraps `directories` (https://codeberg.org/dirs/directories-rs),
version 6.0.0, commit 1f285d9114176e7be8b85b354e3bfde7c3e6356e
(`dirs-sys` 0.5.0), licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0 by the directories-rs
contributors:

  Copyright (c) 2018 directories-rs contributors

Intentional platform divergences from upstream `directories`:

1. Android (`target_os = "android"`):
   Upstream routes Android through `lin.rs` (XDG / `$HOME`), which yields
   `None` or unusable paths inside Android APK sandboxes. `nsh-directories`
   instead queries `android.content.Context` (`getDataDir`, `getFilesDir`,
   `getCacheDir`, `getNoBackupFilesDir`) via `ndk-context` + `jni`, and
   returns `None` for `UserDirs::new()` (Scoped Storage).

2. iOS (`target_os = "ios"`):
   `BaseDirs` and `ProjectDirs` delegate to upstream `mac.rs`. `UserDirs`
   is overridden to expose only `home_dir` and `document_dir`
   (`$HOME/Documents`), returning `None` for desktop-only folders such as
   `Desktop`, `Music`, `Movies`, `Downloads`, `Pictures`, `Public`, and
   `Library/Fonts`.
